  "details": "<p>The temple was worked on by the following Mesopotamian kings: Adad-apla-iddina,\u00a0Hammu-rapi, Kurigalzu, Nebuchadnezzar II, and\u00a0S\u016bm\u00fb-la-El.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The shrine/cella of the god Zababa in the Edubba temple at Kish. The Sumerian ceremonial name Emeteursaga means \"House, Worthy of the Hero.\"",
